### Email Reply Service API Test Requests
### Use with VS Code REST Client, IntelliJ HTTP Client, or similar tools

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@contentType = application/json

### ============================================================================
### Health & Status
### ============================================================================

### Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Get Service Status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/email/status

### Start Email Service
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/email/start
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Stop Email Service
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/email/stop
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### ============================================================================
### Email Verification
### ============================================================================

### Send Verification Email
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/email/verify
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "memberName": "John Doe"
}

### Verify Email Token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/email/verify/{{$random.uuid}}

### ============================================================================
### OTP Password Reset
### ============================================================================

### Request Password Reset OTP
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/otp/request
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "ipAddress": "192.168.1.1"
}

### Verify OTP and Reset Password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/otp/verify
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "otp": "123456",
  "newPassword": "NewSecureP@ssw0rd!",
  "ipAddress": "192.168.1.1"
}

### ============================================================================
### Contribution Reminders
### ============================================================================

### Send Contribution Reminder
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/contribution/remind
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "memberId": 1
}

### ============================================================================
### Dashboard Integration
### ============================================================================

### Request Loan Approval
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/loan/request
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "memberId": 1,
  "amount": 5000,
  "purpose": "Business expansion"
}

### Approve/Reject Loan
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/loan/approve
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "loanId": 1,
  "adminId": 1,
  "approved": true,
  "rejectionReason": "Insufficient funds"
}

### ============================================================================
### Member Approval
### ============================================================================

### Approve/Reject Member
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/member/approve
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "memberId": 1,
  "adminId": 1,
  "approved": true,
  "denialReason": "Incomplete application"
}

### ============================================================================
### SMS Fallback
### ============================================================================

### Send SMS Message
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sms/send
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "phoneNumber": "+1234567890",
  "message": "Your OTP is 123456",
  "priority": "urgent"
}

### ============================================================================
### Analytics
### ============================================================================

### Get Analytics Report (24h)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/analytics?timeRange=24h

### Get Analytics Report (7d)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/analytics?timeRange=7d

### Get All Metrics
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/analytics/metrics

### ============================================================================
### Cache (Redis)
### ============================================================================

### Set Cache Value
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cache/set
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "key": "user:1",
  "value": {
    "name": "John Doe",
    "email": "john@example.com"
  },
  "ttl": 3600
}

### Get Cache Value
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cache/get/user:1

### ============================================================================
### Webhooks
### ============================================================================

### Register Webhook
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/webhook/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "event": "email.sent",
  "url": "https://your-webhook-url.com/webhook",
  "secret": "your-webhook-secret"
}

### Trigger Webhook
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/webhook/trigger
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "event": "email.sent",
  "payload": {
    "email": "user@example.com",
    "subject": "Test Email"
  }
}

### ============================================================================
### Multi-Language
### ============================================================================

### Get Available Languages
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/language/available

### Get Translation (English)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/language/translate/en/greeting.morning

### Get Translation (Spanish)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/language/translate/es/greeting.morning

### Get Translation (French)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/language/translate/fr/greeting.morning

### ============================================================================
### PDF Generation
### ============================================================================

### Generate Loan Statement PDF
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/pdf/loan-statement
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "loanId": 1,
  "memberId": 1
}

### ============================================================================
### Email Tracking
### ============================================================================

### Track Email Open (Tracking Pixel)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/track/open/abc123def456

### ============================================================================
### Test All Endpoints Sequentially
### ============================================================================

### 1. Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 2. Get Status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/email/status

### 3. Send Verification Email
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/email/verify
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "memberName": "Test User"
}

### 4. Request OTP
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/otp/request
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "ipAddress": "127.0.0.1"
}

### 5. Get Analytics
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/analytics

### 6. Set Cache
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cache/set
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "key": "test:key",
  "value": { "test": "data" },
  "ttl": 300
}

### 7. Get Cache
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cache/get/test:key

### 8. Get Languages
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/language/available

### 9. Register Webhook
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/webhook/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "event": "test.event",
  "url": "https://example.com/webhook",
  "secret": "test-secret"
}

### 10. Trigger Webhook
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/webhook/trigger
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "event": "test.event",
  "payload": { "test": true }
}

### ============================================================================
### Error Testing
### ============================================================================

### Invalid Email Format
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/email/verify
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "invalid-email",
  "memberName": "Test User"
}

### Invalid OTP Format
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/otp/verify
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "otp": "12345",
  "newPassword": "Test@123",
  "ipAddress": "127.0.0.1"
}

### Weak Password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/otp/verify
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "otp": "123456",
  "newPassword": "weak",
  "ipAddress": "127.0.0.1"
}

### ============================================================================
### Notes
### ============================================================================
### 
### Testing Instructions:
### 1. Start the server: npm start
### 2. Ensure .env file is configured with your credentials
### 3. Click "Send Request" above each endpoint in VS Code REST Client
### 4. Or use cURL/Postman with the provided URLs
### 
### Prerequisites:
### - Database must be running and configured
### - SMTP credentials must be valid
### - Optional: Redis, Twilio credentials for full testing
### 
### Important:
### - Replace test@example.com with real email addresses for actual testing
### - Use valid database IDs for member/loan endpoints
### - Configure webhook URLs with real endpoints for webhook testing
